#
# Counter-example for gmeow:ModelDeploymentShape: a ModelDeployment realizes AT
# MOST ONE gmeow:deploymentArtifact (a deployment serves one artifact; two
# distinct served models are two deployments). This fixture declares one
# deployment with two gmeow:deploymentArtifact values over one deployment, so
# native SHACL MUST reject it with shacl.MaxCountConstraintComponent. Both
# artifacts are correctly typed gmeow:ModelArtifact so the ONLY violation is the
# cardinality, not a class mismatch.

@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/model-serving/tests/> .

ex:deploymentBad a gmeow:ModelDeployment ;
    gmeow:deploymentArtifact ex:artifactA ;
    gmeow:deploymentArtifact ex:artifactB .   # <-- the second value trips sh:maxCount 1

ex:artifactA a gmeow:ModelArtifact .
ex:artifactB a gmeow:ModelArtifact .
